# Intent: Fast eyes, part 5 (bench builds only). Counters that say why a face is not smooth: every gap of 40 ms or more between two refreshes (under 400 ms, longer is a still face) with what it was made of (the refresh that ended it, what the avatar update held the screen lock for, the rest: the screen task asleep, waiting or pushed aside), the whole time a pass of the update loop held the screen lock, what building a picture costs (avg_pic_ms, pic_per_s), and the A/B switches of one image: self.face.bench_mode sprite_off 1 (shape lists, patch V23), ls_wide 1 (servo and LED buses under the lock, patch V25), one_buffer 1 (one half buffer, patch V26). self.face.bench_run also writes its answer as one FACERUN log line, because the long reply on the cable can be cut by another task's log line. The counter snapshots (four 100 bin histograms) are static, not on the main task's 6 KB stack: with the new counters they overflowed it (found on the unit, 2026-11-16).
# Placement: unit (bench builds only)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_facebench.{cc,h} (ours, patches H01, V20)
# Check after a flash: self.face.bench_run what move answers slow_gaps, avg_hold_ms, avg_pic_ms and writes a FACERUN line; bench_mode one_buffer 1 and 0 switch the draw buffers while the face runs.

